| --- | --- |
| Verse and a second exposition | [Dhammapada](Dhammapada.lingua#r_1Z3DYNZGESCJK781NA8RBA6MBP); [Walpola Rahula](Rahula.lingua#r_6MPM9AYPVMM9JVBVGXF3VVA852) |
| Mindfulness and Theravāda systematisation | [Anālayo](Analayo.lingua#r_4EC9FW4WQZC5FB1WWX92MHR8MQ); [Buddhaghosa](Visuddhimagga.lingua#r_36V0PNBMHFZQ195WQ0X7SMW61J) |
| A modern Vietnamese Zen presentation | [Thich Nhat Hanh](Thich-Nhat-Hanh.lingua#r_1YX8S2K3MFABA4XVQFTC3F7DV6) |
| Mahāyāna ethics and wisdom | [Śāntideva](Bodhisattva.lingua#r_7ZCDQRFNWQVDH1RBH833TZS72T); [Heart Sutra](Heart-sutra.lingua#r_77HWZ92MEFKSM97SD7MN2GD5BR); [Nāgārjuna](Middle-way.lingua#r_2RQKANQG7B3DBTKTES8FRS9573) |
| Scripture and literary teaching | [Lotus Sutra](Lotus.lingua#r_3YS1EP99KTKBTGXKR0XDCBG43K) |
| Modern and classical Japanese Zen | [Suzuki](Zen-mind.lingua#r_1XY4XRP870EMBAEAJQ39WGQ2XZ), then [Dōgen](Dogen.lingua#r_06M92K0Y27WRJY7K34A0YFTDJN) |
